#{[17592186503664 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503664 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503664 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503664 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)$ using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=$\n\n| {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+1$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e63bbce-6bf5-50ed-a823-bd6bd4ad0965" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503664 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}-1}{{e}^{2(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-1}{{e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}}-1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\sqrt{5})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "568ae2e9-d676-5003-b917-02b31b4feb79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503688 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\sqrt{5}}+{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\sqrt{2}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\sqrt{2})=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\,-$ {{field-1}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "57b7ec72-0bfc-579f-8690-12d54f8319d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503689 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\sqrt{2}}-{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3})$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3})=$\n\n| {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n| ${e}^{2k/3}+1$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "957cf846-05af-527e-b9b5-8a808e2c175e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503717 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3}) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(k/3)}-1}{{e}^{2(k/3)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2k/3}-1}{{e}^{2k/3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $z>0,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "958048ce-f9d1-5782-ad7f-1bcc0753619d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503718 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}-{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{z}^{2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{z}^{-2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({z}^{2}-{z}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{z}^{4}-1}{{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{z}^{4}-1}{2{z}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1069 "q-300746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(-\\frac{3x}{4})$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic cosine.\n\n$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(-\\frac{3x}{4})=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98232048-0528-5aa4-8a77-d211e3369a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503719 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(-\\frac{3x}{4}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3x/4}+{e}^{-(-3x/4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3x/4}+{e}^{3x/4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic sine.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x=$\n {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4db71bf-bb20-5cb8-bf0c-68dc6c798e64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503732 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $sinh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3/2}\\,-$ {{field-1}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be80c98f-2a34-525c-9b0c-3079917fdbf6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503737 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sinh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3/2}-{e}^{-3/2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95601" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea77914f-6e86-5cb0-a566-942e82f36dc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503752 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2(-1/2)}}{1+{e}^{-2(-1/2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-e}{1+e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1069 "q-9445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8cf4372-3ba4-555f-93d2-c874764a61de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503756 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\sqrt{3}}-1}{{e}^{2\\sqrt{3}}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
